  "body": "According to the <html> element's spec, \"An html element's start tag can be omitted if the first thing inside the html element is not a comment.\" But it also says that \"Authors are encouraged to specify a lang attribute on the root html element, giving the document's language.\" So, the spec is contradictory, because we can't give document's language without html element.\r\n\r\nMost web developer chose not to omit the starting tag to add lang attribute, since without it, the page might be interpreted as foreign language. I know so many Japanese sites misinterpreted as Chinese just because they lack the attribute.\r\n\r\nBecause of that, we must decrare html element's start tag ( which follow suit the conventional practice), or somehow we need to find the way to specify the html file's language.",
